1
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:02,660
当然，每一波浪潮都不一样，
Of course, every wave is different,

2
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:09,000
但这一波，和我们迄今经历过的任何一波，都非常不同。
but this wave is unusually different than anything we have experienced so far.

3
00:00:10,110 --> 00:00:12,500
今天学到的，明天就没用了。
Whatever you learn today is useless tomorrow.

4
00:00:13,350 --> 00:00:14,950
你积累不下来。
You don't accumulate.

5
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:18,750
于是，你越来越依赖外物。
And so you rely more and more into impersonal.

6
00:00:19,010 --> 00:00:21,650
你买更大的电脑，现在又用上了 AI，
You get a bigger computer, now you use AI,

7
00:00:22,310 --> 00:00:25,750
当然，到某个时候，你就会被取代。
and of course, you'll be replaced at some point.

8
00:00:43,420 --> 00:00:49,180
我常说：如果你能以可持续的方式，让知识复利增长，
And I always say, look, if you can compound your knowledge in a sustainable fashion,

9
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:52,700
最终，你的资本也能复利增长。
eventually you can compound your capital as well.

10
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,540
复利的基本理念，是不要失去你已经拥有的。
And the basic idea of compounding is you don't lose what you already have.

11
00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:02,160
这是一个深刻的道理。
And that's a profound idea.

12
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:05,060
不要失去你已经拥有的——
You don't lose what you already have.

13
00:01:05,180 --> 00:01:06,900
包括你的知识，
That's including your knowledge,

14
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:10,160
包括你基于信任的关系，
that's including your trusting relationship,

15
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,650
包括你的智慧，甚至你的健康。
that's including your wisdom and even your health.

16
00:01:18,770 --> 00:01:20,070
你只需要富一次。
You only have to get rich once.

17
00:01:20,290 --> 00:01:23,910
为什么有些人——非常聪明的人——
And why do people, very bright people,

18
00:01:24,710 --> 00:01:29,410
会拿对自己非常重要的东西去冒险，只为得到完全不重要的东西？
risk losing something that's very important to them to gain something that's totally unimportant?

19
00:01:29,490 --> 00:01:32,110
多赚的钱，毫无用处；
The added money has no utility whatsoever.

20
00:01:33,050 --> 00:01:36,290
而亏掉的钱，却极其重要。
And the money that was lost had enormous utility.

21
00:01:38,650 --> 00:01:43,890
甚至可以说，如果你不能心平气和地面对
In fact, you can argue that if you're not willing to react with equanimity

22
00:01:43,910 --> 00:01:51,050
每个世纪两三次、市价下跌 50% 的情况，
to a market price decline of 50% two or three times a century,

23
00:01:51,090 --> 00:01:56,150
你就不适合做普通股股东，你也只配得到平庸的结果。
you're not fit to be a common shareholder, and you deserve the mediocre result you're going to get

24
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:01,740
复利的本质，就像一个沾着湿雪的雪球。
The nature of compound interest is it behaves like a snowball of sticky snow.

25
00:02:03,660 --> 00:02:09,300
诀窍是要有一道很长的坡——要么很早开始，要么活得足够久。
The trick is to have a very long hill, which means either starting very young or living to be very old.

26
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:14,680
我不断看到一些人在人生中崛起，
I constantly see people rise in life

27
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:22,720
他们不是最聪明的，有时甚至不是最勤奋的，但他们是「学习机器」。
who were not the smartest, sometimes not even the most diligent, but they are learning machines.

28
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:27,920
他们每晚睡觉时，都比早上起床时更聪明一点。
They go to bed every night a little wiser than they were when they got up.

29
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:35,880
这个习惯太有用了——尤其当你前面还有很长的路要走。
And boy, does that habit help, particularly when you have a long run ahead of you.

30
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:49,437
每年 +10%，30 年后是 17.4 倍。每年 −10%，只剩 4%。

31
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:10,280
一次永久性的腰斩（−50%），需要翻倍（+100%）才能回到原点。按每年 10% 计算，要 7 年多。

32
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:21,012
只要价值仍在、不被迫卖出，暂时的下跌可以等待；真正改写结果的，是不可逆的损失。

33
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:28,266
金钱如此，知识、信任、技能与健康，也是如此。

34
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:38,193
在变化的世界里，持续积累真正有价值的东西，并尽可能避免不可逆的损失。

35
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:43,878
变化越快，越需要知道，什么值得长期积累。

